> Retain the original thirty-variable ZDT1 experiment

ZDT1 uses f1=x0, g=1+9 times the mean of the remaining coordinates, and f2=g
times(1−sqrt(f1/g)) on the unit box. Its analytic front has all remaining
coordinates zero, hence g=1 and f2=1−sqrt(f1). The native benchmark validates
dimensions and unit-box inputs, and the analytic front helper provides the
reference curve.

The original run uses30 variables,100 requested weights, neighborhood20,250
generations, default variation settings, Tchebycheff decomposition and seed1.
The returned set is the non-dominated subset of the final population, with
identical non-dominated duplicates retained. Its vertical gap is
f2−(1−sqrt(f1)); the mean does not measure front coverage or hypervolume. The
table reports first-objective coverage separately. All values below come from
this checkout rather than the old frozen claim of a particular gap.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/moead_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/optim/moead.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::optim::MOEADOptions o;
    o.seed = 1;
    dm::optim::ZDT1Objective f;
    auto front =
        dm::optim::MOEAD(o).optimize(f, std::vector<double>(30, 0),
                                     std::vector<double>(30, 1));
    auto s = dm::optim::zdt1_front_summary(front);
    std::vector<double> x, y, tx, ty;
    for (auto &p : front) {
        x.push_back(p.objectives[0]);
        y.push_back(p.objectives[1]);
    }
    for (auto &p : dm::optim::zdt1_front()) {
        tx.push_back(p.objectives[0]);
        ty.push_back(p.objectives[1]);
    }
    std::print("| returned points incl duplicates | min f1 | max f1 | mean vertical gap | max vertical gap " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               s.points, s.min_f1, s.max_f1, s.mean_gap, s.max_gap);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(tx, ty, "analytic ZDT1 front", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(
        x, y, "actual native approximation", {37, 99, 235}, 5).title(
        "Original ZDT1: native final approximation").x_label("objective1").y_label("objective2").save_svg("build/moead_original.svg");
}
```
