> Finite prefixes and complete cost accounting

Repeated runs with the same seed and options, changing only the generation cap,
share the same trajectory prefix on this toolchain. Their returned fronts can
change in size and coverage, and their mean gap need not improve monotonically.
The finite sweep below compares those actual end states without claiming
convergence from a visual trend.

The implementation first evaluates one random probe solely to discover objective
count. It discards that point and does not include it in the ideal.
Initialization then evaluates N points and each generation evaluates N more:
exactly1+N+G*N successful callbacks. This extra probe matters for stateful or
expensive objectives. Neighbor setup compares weight distances while sorting all
N candidates per slot, with O(m*N squared log N) coarse work, and final
non-dominated extraction costs O(m*N squared). A generation uses O(N*(n+T*m))
work excluding callback and variation details; describing only neighborhood
updates would omit setup, variation and output filtering.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/moead_prefixes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/optim/moead.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| generations | callbacks by exact schedule | returned points | min f1 | max f1 | actual " "mean gap |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t g : {0U, 5U, 25U, 100U, 250U}) {
        dm::optim::MOEADOptions o;
        o.seed = 1;
        o.max_generations = g;
        dm::optim::ZDT1Objective f;
        auto front =
            dm::optim::MOEAD(o).optimize(f, std::vector<double>(30, 0),
                                         std::vector<double>(30, 1));
        auto s = dm::optim::zdt1_front_summary(front);
        x.push_back(g);
        y.push_back(s.mean_gap);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", g, 1 + 100 + 100 * g,
                   s.points, s.min_f1, s.max_f1, s.mean_gap);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "mean vertical gap", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "ZDT1: actual fixed-seed generation prefixes").x_label(
        "completed generations").y_label("mean vertical gap of returned front").save_svg("build/moead_prefixes.svg");
}
```
